course: dictionary
lesson: 2476
title: One word, many days
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word day has many meanings, so look at the words around it to find the right one. In «Mercury goes around in 88 days», day means a unit of time: the time from one midnight to the next, which has 24 hours. Seven days make a week.
explain: In «there is at least one day a year when the Sun does not set», day means something different: the time when it is light and not night, so the Sun stays up for a long time.
explain: In «in those days», day means a time or age. In «sports day» and «a day off», day means a special day. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found it.
explain: Some day words are casual. «G'day» is a greeting in Australia, «call it a day» means stop working, and «make my day» means make me very happy. In exams you may see «per day», «daily» or «on a daily basis», which all mean every day.
fact: A day is the time from one midnight to the next, and it has 24 hours.
fact: Seven days make a week.
fact: The Earth turns once in a day, which is why we have day and night.
fact: «Day» can also mean the light part of the day, when it is not night.
fact: «G'day» is a casual greeting used in Australia, and «call it a day» means stop working.
exercise: «Next day he asks politely and plays where they put him.» What does next day mean? | A special day, like sports day | *The following day | The light part of the day | A greeting
exercise: What does «a day off» mean? | A day of rain | A day in the past | A day with the lights on | *A special day when you do not have to work or go to school
exercise: «A week has seven days.» How many hours are in one day? | 7 hours | 12 hours | *24 hours | 60 hours
test: «Inside the Arctic Circle, there is at least one day a year when the Sun does not set.» What does day mean here? | A special day, like sports day | *The time from one midnight to the next, with 24 hours | A greeting | A time or age, like in those days
test: Which place uses «G'day» as a greeting? | Mexico | Scotland | *Australia | The southern US
exam: Exams say «per day» and «on a daily basis». Which phrase means the same? | Once a week | *Each day | At night | Long ago
